Veyon for Debian/Ubuntu
-----------------------

The upstream release tarball is repacked without code for MS Windows and
Android, without prebuilt Windows binaries and without the embedded copies of
libraries that the package takes from the distribution (see Files-Excluded in
debian/copyright). In particular the VNC server of Veyon Server on X11 is the
x11vnc program of the x11vnc package (-DVEYON_X11VNC_EXTERNAL=ON), and
LibVNCServer/LibVNCClient come from libvncserver.

Since Veyon 4.11:

 * veyon-auth-helper (used by logon authentication) is a D-Bus activated
   systemd service (veyon-auth-helper.service, io.veyon.AuthHelper on the
   system bus) and no longer setuid root. Upgrading from an older package
   removes the dpkg-statoverride that made it setuid.

 * veyon-input-helper blocks the keyboard and mouse during a screen lock in
   Wayland sessions only (X11 sessions do not use it). Upstream installs it
   setuid root; this package does not, so on X11-only systems there is no
   setuid program. To use input blocking in Wayland sessions, make it setuid:

     dpkg-statoverride --update --add root root 4755 /usr/bin/veyon-input-helper

 * veyon.service is not enabled by the package. Enable it once Veyon is
   configured (veyon-cli and veyon-configurator do so when they save the
   configuration and Service/Autostart is on, the default):

     systemctl enable --now veyon.service

 -- Vietnam Linux Family <developer@vietnamlinuxfamily.net>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0700

DFSG-FREE PACKAGE
-----------------

The SHA-1 implementation in upstream sources (ica/x11/common/sha1.{h,c})
is directly taken from RFC 3174 "US Secure Hash Algorithm 1 (SHA1)". Given
that Debian considers RFCs non-free according to the Debian Free Software
Guidelines 3 and 6, the offending files have been removed from the upstream
sources.

Luckily, the SHA-1 implementation provided by the OpenSSL library is compatible
with the own in Bacula.  The fact that iTALC is already linked against OpenSSL
also means that nothing changed for the Debian package.

This change was introduced with Debian upload of italc 2.0.2+dfsg1-2.

